-- NorthstarIQ — Governed lifecycle transition history, and what is absent from it
--
-- ⚠️ LATER-CREATED REPRODUCIBILITY EVIDENCE — written 2026-09-01 AFTER the
-- controlled lifecycle validation. It was NOT used during that validation and
-- is not historical evidence. It exists so the transition trail can be re-read.
--
-- Purpose: Lead Status field history is the retained transition trail. This
-- query reads it for the controlled fixtures.
--
-- THE ABSENCE IS THE EVIDENCE. During the controlled run four unsupported saves
-- were deliberately attempted against NIQ Fixture 01 — an unsupported lifecycle
-- transition, an unsupported MQL qualification, an unsupported Sales acceptance,
-- and an unsupported SQL qualification. Each was refused by a Custom Error and
-- the whole transaction rolled back. NONE of them appears in this result, and
-- none ever will: a before-save rejection writes no history row.
--
-- ⚠️ DO NOT READ A REJECTED ATTEMPT AS A DETECTED DEFECT. The rejected states
-- never persisted, so NorthstarIQ had nothing to detect afterwards. This query
-- can show that a forbidden transition is ABSENT; it cannot show that anything
-- caught one.
--
-- Observed 2026-09-01: NIQ Fixture 01 showed the complete governed chain
--   Open - Not Contacted → Working - Contacted → MQL → SAL → SQL
--   → Closed - Converted (written by native Salesforce Lead Conversion)
-- with no forbidden transition present. Historical execution evidence.
--
-- ⚠️ Salesforce field history is bounded and never records a Lead's INITIAL
-- status, so an absent row is not proof a transition never happened on an older
-- record. That limitation is why Lifecycle Progression Integrity reports
-- Unable to Determine rather than Failed where nothing retained can settle it.
--
-- Read-only. Safe to run against any org.

SELECT LeadId,
       Lead.Company,
       Lead.Status,
       Field,
       OldValue,
       NewValue,
       CreatedDate
FROM LeadHistory
WHERE Lead.Company LIKE 'NIQ Fixture%'
  AND Field = 'Status'
ORDER BY LeadId, CreatedDate
